==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cooldown Equality}}

==Battleground==
*1 [[Mistress Celeboodle]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*2 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Ursamajor]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Nimoy Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns.
**8 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**8 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 133.33~136.67 seconds<sup>4,000f~4,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Welcome to Cooldown Equality! Due to CD being 16 for every unit, many levels involve spamming strong generalist Ubers or units with very long CDs with great stats/utility.

However, traditional meatshield spam is now harder, as their 16 cooldowns are not worth the little health they have. Instead, tankers are much better here, as they often have longer cooldowns with high amounts of HP.

A [[Battle Items|Rich Cat]] may be nice so you don't accidentally drain your cash.

This stage features Mistress Celeboodles and Mooths as money bags, while the Nimoy Bore, Ursamajors, and ocassional Aku Gories will mercilessly plow through your units if you are not careful. To top it all off, a Professor A. is there to kill any units that push too far.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: With the Extra Money talent, Can Can Cat can kill the Mistress Celeboodles if protected, giving you a lot of money to spend on harder hitting units. Can also be used to hit the Nimoy Bore occassionaly, but can't do much against Ursamajor or Professor A. Can Can Cat's cooldown is relatively the same here, so it doesn't get held back or benefited from the gimmick.
*[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]: A good tank against Ursamajor and Nimoy Bore, especially due to their cooldown reduction. However, the Aku Gories will plow through them.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: Extremely HP for such a cheap cost, can temporarily stall enemies.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Due to their heavily decreased cooldowns, both units can be stacked easily, preventing any of the main threats from moving so backliners can chip them down. Be sure to protect them well, as any attack will kill them here.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer Cat's cooldown is actually slightly reduced here, so they are able to create a potent stack against the Nimoy Bore easily with enough luck. It struggles at hitting Ursamajor unless timed well, and is rendered useless against Professor A.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Can use Nimoy Bore and potentially Mistress Celeboodle as stepping stones for its waves. However, it cannot do much when Professor A. or Ursamajor are in the front. Their cooldown remains relatively the same, so you are free to spam it.

